WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:01.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our next guest is a hilarious
comedian, writer,

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:04.904
and Emmy-nominated host
of the Netflix show "Nailed It!"

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
She also hosts
the TBS show "Wipeout,"

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.676 size:88% position:44%
as well as the podcast
"Why Won't You Date Me?"

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:11.177 line:92%
Please welcome back to the sho

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:13.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of our favorites,
Nicole Byer.

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:14.614 size:75% position:38% line:92%
How are you, Nicole?

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.182 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Hi, Seth, how are you?

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:18.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm wonderful, and I
desperately want to talk to yo

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:22.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
about your television show
but I am also aware

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:24.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you have
a different TV show

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:25.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you are currently
obsessed with.

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
Could you tell us
a little about that?

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:31.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am obsessed
with Tyler Perry's "The Oval."

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:32.866 line:92%
Okay, Seth, have you seen it

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:35.168 line:92%
-I did not know it existed

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:37.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, so,
it's a White House drama.

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:41.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
He rebuilt the White House
80% to scale.

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:43.810 size:81% position:41%
And then in the pilot,
a kid gets kidnapped.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:47.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a cult. There's
cheating. There's slapping

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:48.848 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It is honestly --

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:51.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a wild ride.
I love it so much.

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:55.121
-How many episodes of "The Oval"
have happened?

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:58.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh, Tyler Perry works
very fast, very, very fast

00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:01.528
I think there's like 30 episodes
or something like that.

00:01:01.528 --> 00:01:04.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's only happened
within like the last two years

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:07.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's truly so wild.
-God, I love him.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.803 line:92%
It's just amazing what he does

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:10.370 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-He's incredible.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:13.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
I worship at the altar
of Tyler Perry!

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:16.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, we worship
at the altar of Nicole Bye

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:17.410 line:92%
over here at "Late Night."

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
You are hosting "Wipeout"
right now.

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:22.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is people
with far too much confidence

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they can complete
an obstacle course.

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:30.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you even gone near trying
to do the course yourself?

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:30.590 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-So, I asked.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:33.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
Before we started,
I said, "Please let me do it

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:33.993 size:78% position:39% line:92%
It will be so funny."

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:36.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then three weeks
before we started shooting

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:40.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
I fell down my stairs
and dislocated my ankle.

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.168 line:92%
My foot was, like, on backwards.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:45.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they were like,
"Nicole, that's a no.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:46.139 line:92%
You can't even walk down stairs.

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:48.975
What makes you think you can d
a full-blown obstacle course?"

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:51.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like "Uh-huh, yeah
you guys are right."

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:53.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, there should be
a different show

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:57.183 size:84% position:42%
called "Light Wipeout,"
which is just stairs,

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:59.319 line:92%
a rug on a slippery floor.

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:01.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's just, like,
walking in heels.

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:02.555 line:92%
It's like, "Can you do it?

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:04.190 size:88% position:44% line:92%
The answer for me is no.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:07.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wait. You fell off
a motorcycle, though.

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:08.695 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What was that?

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:11.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. So, I fell
off a motorcycle twice.

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:12.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of my dear friends,
Meatball --

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:15.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's a drag queen. That's not
her government name --

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:16.736 line:92%
But she's got a motorcycle

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:17.604 line:92%
She was like, "Nicole, get on.

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:19.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, "Okay."
And I was doing really well,

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:23.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the last thing I heard was
"Diva, you're killing it."

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:24.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I just
took this turn too hard.

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:27.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"I'm crashing into a fence."

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.149 line:92%
And then I heard, "Diva, no!

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:32.886 size:88% position:44%
And then the second time
was during my road test.

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:37.323
If you fall off a motorcycle
during your road test, you fail.

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:37.924 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That seems fair.

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:40.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you actually went so far
after your first fall

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.595 line:92%
to try to get a license for it

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:44.964 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah, and then after
I fell the second time,

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:45.899 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I bought a motorcycle.

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:48.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, is my brain
working correctly?

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:49.502 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We'll never know.

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:53.039
-Have you always been interested
in motorcycles and cars?

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:55.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. When I was a kid, I
wanted to be, like, a mechanic

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:58.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
or, like, a very sassy
bus driver with long nails

00:02:58.478 --> 00:03:01.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'd be like, "Beep, beep
get on the bus!"

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:02.649 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:02.649 --> 00:03:05.351 line:92%
-Now, probably not a school bus.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:10.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
As we have discussed before,
children like you.

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:13.993 line:92%
You do not care for children

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:14.561 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No.

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:17.096 line:92%
Uh, no offense. They're sticky

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:19.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're very dumb.
Like, that's not me being rude

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:22.769 size:81% position:41%
You literally have to
teach kids everything.

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:24.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
Otherwise,
they don't know anything.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:26.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I keep getting booked
on these things.

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:27.674 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I'm doing "Rugrats."

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:28.675 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Kids love "Nailed It!"

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:30.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm doing a lot
of cartoon voices.

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:33.713
I don't know. Maybe I'm going to
have to learn to love kids

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:34.480 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I don't want to.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What shows did you watch
as a kids?

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:37.884 line:92%
Were you a "Rugrats" fan?

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:39.285 line:92%
-I was not a "Rugrats" fan

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:40.353 line:92%
I didn't have cable growing up

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:42.589
So, if I went to a friends
house, and "Rugrats" was on,

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:46.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd be like, "Oh, wow.
This is luxury. I love this.

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:49.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I was a kid, I watche
what my mom watched,

00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:52.565 line:92%
and she loved "Ally McBeal."

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:54.033 line:92%
Loved. Like, I just discovered

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:56.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the dancing baby
was not just a dancing baby --

00:03:56.703 --> 00:04:00.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a woman wanting a baby.
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:02.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"Ooh, this baby fun."

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:05.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You also have a podcast calle
"Why Won't You Date Me?"

00:04:05.245 --> 00:04:08.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think a lot of peopl
are very excited

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:09.716 line:92%
for what dating might look lik

00:04:09.716 --> 00:04:11.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
now that we are
getting our vaccines,

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:14.687 size:84% position:42%
now that we can have
physical contact again.

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:18.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you excited
about what's next?

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:20.126 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I am so excited.

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:23.429 size:81% position:41%
I am fully vaccinated.
I have no standards.

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:25.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
This summer,
I want every hole filled.

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:28.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is it. That's just --
That's what I want.

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:30.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
All of them. I don't want
to be able to speak!

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:34.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you for using
your "Rugrats" catchphrase

00:04:34.674 --> 00:04:36.709 line:92%
"I want every hole filled.

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:39.512 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:46.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
God, please don't let the kids
connect the dots now.

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:48.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's very --
Another thing that's excitin

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:52.859
is getting up, doing stand-u
in front of audiences again.

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:55.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
Seems like that's
going to start happening.

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:58.598
Are you excited?
Are you worried you'll be rusty?

00:04:58.598 --> 00:05:01.100 size:78% position:39%
-I'm a little worried
about being rusty.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:04.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I've, like, been going
through my sets, transcribing.

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
The thing I'm, like,
most afraid of

00:05:05.405 --> 00:05:08.308
is people during meet-and-greets
wanting to touch me.

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:11.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
I like the bubble.
I like the six feet away.

00:05:11.044 --> 00:05:13.746 line:92%
I like masks. Don't touch me

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:17.250
-That seems very at odds
with the last thing you told us.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.251 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:21.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Unless you filling something,
stay away from me!

00:05:21.321 --> 00:05:23.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
You know, I will tell you,

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:26.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did a little stand-up
a couple weeks ago.

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:28.428 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And it's so thrilling

00:05:28.428 --> 00:05:34.133 size:84% position:42%
how excited people are
to just watch anything.

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:36.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I don't know
if I was any good.

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:39.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
People were just
so thirsty for content.

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:39.939 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:43.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, I've done a couple
outdoor shows, and people --

00:05:43.176 --> 00:05:45.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
They get excited,
and then they're just, like,

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:47.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
willing to listen,
which is so nice.

00:05:47.747 --> 00:05:49.716 line:92%
-Yeah. It's also so nice,

00:05:49.716 --> 00:05:51.651 size:75% position:38%
because I feel like,
during the pandemic,

00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:54.754 size:81% position:41%
you would tell people
how your pandemic was,

00:05:54.754 --> 00:05:57.390 size:88% position:44%
and then you'd have to
listen to them tell you.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:59.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
And with stand-up,
you just get to tell them.

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:02.061
-Which I love.
The last show I did, I was like,

00:06:02.061 --> 00:06:04.731
"We're going to talk about 2020,
'cause it ruined my life.

00:06:04.731 --> 00:06:06.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was very awful,
and you have to listen."

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:08.234 line:92%
And they were like, "Yes!"

00:06:08.234 --> 00:06:10.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"This is perfect.

00:06:10.403 --> 00:06:12.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a dream."
It's like therapy

00:06:12.105 --> 00:06:14.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
but with a bunch of people
who don't talk back.

00:06:14.107 --> 00:06:18.277
-Well, it is always like therapy
for us to see you, as well

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:21.647
We do hope that you will make it
back here into our studio

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:22.281 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
one of these days.

00:06:22.281 --> 00:06:24.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
And thank you so much
for making the time for us

00:06:24.584 --> 00:06:26.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Aww, Seth, thank you
for having me.

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:27.387 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
This is a treat.

00:06:27.387 --> 00:06:30.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A special live version
of "Why Won't You Date Me?

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:33.159 size:84% position:42%
is available on-demand
for the next seven days

00:06:33.159 --> 00:06:36.629 line:92%
at live.nicolebyerwastaken.com

